athacademy/question-capture/13953040/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-115238" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce6fd9130710f6f82288974366e6ed398a205420c8d0ca28f3d611f8be15c012" "basis" 615 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-115238" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce6fd9130710f6f82288974366e6ed398a205420c8d0ca28f3d611f8be15c012" "basis" 615 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953040/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-50041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}+x+1}{{x}^{2}(x+1)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{C}{x+1},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, determine the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-50041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by ${x}^{2}(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+x+1 & =Ax(x+1)+B(x+1)+C{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(0)^{2}+0+1 & =A(0)(0+1)+B(0+1)+C(0)^{2} \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-1)^{2}+(-1)+1 & =A(-1)(-1+1)+B(-1+1)+C(-1)^{2} \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=1$ and using our values for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(1)^{2}+1+1 & =A(1)(1+1)+(1)(1+1)+(3)(1)^{2} \\\\ 5 & =2A+2+3 \\\\ 5 & =2A+5 \\\\ A & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B\\cdot C=0\\cdot 1\\cdot 3=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-50041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2a1a918b159066bbe9f8412341b3b054e8fdc5b1cd925de5ec26478576b6aec3"} {"question" "q-50041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-50041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-14"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-50041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-70011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+1}{{x}^{3}(x+1)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{D}{x+1},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ are real constants, determine the value of $AB-CD.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-70011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by ${x}^{3}(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+x+1=A{x}^{2}(x+1)+Bx(x+1)+C(x+1)+D{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{2}+(-1)+1 & =A(-1)^{2}(-1+1)+B(-1)(-1+1)+C(-1+1)+D(-1)^{3} \\\\ 1-1+1 & =-D \\\\ 1 & =-D \\\\ D & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}+0+1 & =A(0)^{2}(0+1)+B(0)(0+1)+C(0+1)+D(0)^{3} \\\\ 1 & =C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$ and using our values for $C$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}^{2}+1+1 & =A(1)^{2}(1+1)+B(1)(1+1)+1(1+1)+(-1)(1)^{3} \\\\ 1+1+1 & =2A+2B+2-1 \\\\ 2B & =2-2A \\\\ B & =1-A.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=2$ and using our values for $C$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{2}+2+1 & =A(2)^{2}(2+1)+B(2)(2+1)+1(2+1)+(-1)(2)^{3} \\\\ 4+2+1 & =12A+6B+3-8 \\\\ 6B & =12-12A \\\\ B & =2-2A.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-A & =2-2A \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $A$ into $(1)$  to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\nB=1-1=0\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nAB-CD=1(0)-1(-1)=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-70011" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2a1a918b159066bbe9f8412341b3b054e8fdc5b1cd925de5ec26478576b6aec3"} {"question" "q-70011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-70011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-70011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-73382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-x+4}{(x+2)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x+2}+\\frac{B}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x+2)^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$ and $C$ are real constants, find the value of $A\\cdot B+C.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-73382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+2)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-x+4 & =A(x+2)^{2}+B(x+2)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-2$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{2}-(-2)+4 & =A(-2+2)^{2}+B(-2+2)+C \\\\ 10 & =A(0)+B(0)+C \\\\ C & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0)^{2}-(0)+4 & =A(0+2)^{2}+B(0+2)+10 \\\\ 4 & =4A+2B+10 \\\\ 0 & =4A+2B+6 \\\\ 0 & =2A+B+3 \\\\ B & =-2A-3.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=-1$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{2}-(-1)+4 & =A(-1+2)^{2}+B(-1+2)+10 \\\\ 6 & =A+B+10 \\\\ 0 & =A+B+4 \\\\ B & =-4-A.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2A-3 & =-4-A \\\\ -A & =-1 \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $A$ into $(2)$  to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =-4-1=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cdot B+C & =1\\cdot (-5)+10 \\\\  & =-5+10 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-73382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2a1a918b159066bbe9f8412341b3b054e8fdc5b1cd925de5ec26478576b6aec3"} {"question" "q-73382" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-73382" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-73382" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-115238" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+17x+8}{x(x+2)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x+2}+\\frac{C}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{D}{(x+2)^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ are real constants, determine the value of $AB+CD.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-115238" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $x(x+2)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+17x+8=A(x+2)^{3}+Bx(x+2)^{2}+Cx(x+2)+Dx.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-2$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{3}+8(-2)^{2}+17(-2)+8 & =A(-2+2)^{3}+B(-2)(-2+2)^{2}+C(-2)(-2+2)+D(-2) \\\\ -8+32-34+8 & =-2D \\\\ -8+32-34+8 & =-2D \\\\ -2 & =-2D \\\\ D & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{3}+8(0)^{2}+17(0)+8 & =A(0+2)^{3}+B(0)(0+2)^{2}+C(0)(0+2)+D(0) \\\\ 8 & =8A \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{3}+8(-1)^{2}+17(-1)+8 & =1(-1+2)^{3}+B(-1)(-1+2)^{2}+C(-1)(-1+2)+1(-1) \\\\ -1+8-17+8 & =1-B-C-1 \\\\ B & =2-C.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=-3$ and using our values for $A$ and $D$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)^{3}+8(-3)^{2}+17(-3)+8 & =1(-3+2)^{3}+B(-3)(-3+2)^{2}+C(-3)(-3+2)+1(-3) \\\\ -27+72-51+8 & =-1-3B+3C-3 \\\\ 3B & =3C-6 \\\\ B & =C-2.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-C & =C-2 \\\\ -2C & =-4 \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $C$ into $(1)$  to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\nB=2-2=0\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nAB+CD=1(0)+2(1)=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-115238" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2a1a918b159066bbe9f8412341b3b054e8fdc5b1cd925de5ec26478576b6aec3"} {"question" "q-115238" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-115238" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-115238" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-346806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{x+3}{(x+2)^{2}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{x+3}{(x+2)^{2}}=$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x+2$ |  | $(x+2)^{2}$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-346806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+3}{(x+2)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+2}+\\frac{B}{(x+2)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the above equality by $(x+2)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\nx+3=A(x+2)+B.\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2+3 & =A(-2+2)+B \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+3 & =A(0+2)+1 \\\\ 3 & =2A+1 \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{(x+2)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{x+2}+\\frac{1}{(x+2)^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbfe7079679d09a54855f7d494ac1ae9484703b7bcbfdba68342d6c89fc6f769"} {"question" "q-346806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063513/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2a1a918b159066bbe9f8412341b3b054e8fdc5b1cd925de5ec26478576b6aec3"} {"question" "q-346806" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacade